{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509972-question-about-dragon-dance-yang-parna-\u2022\u2022\u2022-kuei-jin","id":1509972,"title":"Question about Dragon Dance (Yang Parna \u2022\u2022\u2022) - Kuei-jin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-28T11:34:41-07:00","id":1509972,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Question about Dragon Dance (Yang Parna \u2022\u2022\u2022) - Kuei-jin","content":"The book states the following:<br /> <span style=\"color:#e67e22\">&quot;The vampire spends a point of Yang Chi. No roll is needed. While engrossed in the Dragon Dance, the vampire is considered to be in a controlled form of fire soul. All difficulties to influence or control the vampire increase by one. The vampire suffers no wound penalties, and he may add attack successes of a Brawl, Martial Arts or Melee maneuver to his damage Dice Pool, as if the attack were from a firearm.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> I wonder what exactly does it mean, because technically you are already supposed to add successes of a Brawl/Martial Arts/Melee to your damage dice pool.<br /> e.g you have scored 4 successes on punching someone, you take those 4 successes, add your Strength rating on top of that - and roll damage.<br /> So if your Strength was 3 you will have a total of 7 damage dice pool. So I wonder what is the difference?<br /> <br /> My best assumption would be that they meant that the successes accumulated on the roll itself will apply like Automatic Successes of Potence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T15:19:41-07:00","id":1509997,"title":"","content":"This is a 2E Vampire quirk. Bonus successes on the attack roll didn't apply to melee damage, only to ranged attacks. I'd just mod it to say that all his brawl, martial arts and melee manouvers are rolled at -1 difficulty while under the effect if you're using revised/V20 rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T16:00:54-07:00","id":1510002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1509972-question-about-dragon-dance-yang-parna-\u2022\u2022\u2022-kuei-jin?p=1509997#post1509997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a 2E Vampire quirk. Bonus successes on the attack roll didn't apply to melee damage, only to ranged attacks. I'd just mod it to say that all his brawl, martial arts and melee manouvers are rolled at -1 difficulty while under the effect if you're using revised/V20 rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for clarifying!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}